# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and on checkout.
# This overrides core.autocrlf and ensures consistency between Windows
# dev environments and Linux CI runners.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files — never apply line-ending conversion
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.nupkg binary

# Cross-client conformance harnesses — real code we wrote, but not part of the shipped
# product and not built by any CI workflow. Marking them undetectable keeps GitHub's
# language detection (and everything downstream of it) on the C# this repository actually
# ships, instead of inferring Java/Python/JavaScript from 8 files of manual test scaffolding.
#
# EXPERIMENT, and the PR that introduces this is the test: GitHub's Code Quality scan runs
# `Analyze (java-kotlin)`, `Analyze (python)` and `Analyze (javascript-typescript)` on every
# push here — ~2m20s of runner time — solely because these three directories exist. If those
# jobs disappear from this PR's checks, the attribute is doing the job. If they do not,
# revert this block: Code Quality does not read linguist attributes and the languages have
# to be turned off in repository settings instead.
tests/olingo/**   linguist-detectable=false
tests/pyodata/**  linguist-detectable=false
tests/k6/**       linguist-detectable=false
